      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Agree with the pass: Muster Rolls and GAR Membership Records (the two the test requires) are present, and the military rows lead. Genealogist's note: with two of eight slots unused, '1890 Veterans Schedules of the U.S. Federal Census' (a buildable Ancestry row that lists surviving Union veterans and their units) would have served this Civil War soldier better than the undated 1860 census. Not scored down, because the test calls it fitting rather than required, and the 1860 census does place a man in the county before the war."
    },
